course: dictionary
lesson: 5819
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary gives each meaning its own number. Magnolia can be a tree, a flower or a colour. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer means. «Arguing over paint colours like "Magnolia" or "Duck Egg Blue" is a small disagreement about taste, not a real fight, and it ends with a choice or a compromise.» People argue over paint, so magnolia here is a paint colour.
explain: Look for clues. Paint, walls and colours point to the colour meaning. A tree would not be painted. Ask yourself: what is this sentence about? Then choose the meaning that fits, and swap it into the sentence to check.
explain: Magnolia can also describe things, as in «magnolia walls». Here it works like an adjective, and it means the pale, creamy-white colour. Some people use magnolia walls to mean a plain, safe room with no bold colour.
fact: A magnolia is a tree or bush with large, beautiful flowers.
fact: Magnolia flowers can be white, pink or purple, and they often open in spring before the leaves appear.
fact: Magnolia is also a pale, creamy-white colour, often used for painting walls.
fact: Magnolias are one of the oldest kinds of flowering tree.
exercise: In «Arguing over paint colours like "Magnolia" or "Duck Egg Blue" is a small disagreement about taste», what is magnolia? | A bird that sings in spring | *A pale paint colour | A large pink flower | A tree in a garden
exercise: The magnolia opened its big pink flowers in April, before its leaves came out. What is a magnolia here? | A colour for painting walls | *A tree or bush | A kind of bird | A rude or unfriendly person
exercise: Ella says the room has magnolia walls. What might that suggest? | *A plain, safe colour | Bright, loud stripes | A room made of glass | A room full of music
test: Which meaning of magnolia fits this sentence? «The magnolia in the park was covered in white flowers.» | A dull grey stone | A creamy-white paint | *A tree or bush | A plain, boring room
test: Dad says he will paint the kitchen magnolia. What does magnolia mean here? | A flower that smells sweet | A tall, thin tree | A kind of bird | *A pale creamy-white colour
exam: Jayden says a word can have more than one meaning. What should he do? | Always pick the first meaning in the dictionary | Guess at random without reading the sentence | *Use the words around it to choose the meaning that fits | Stop reading the text until he finds the word
